1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,241
A theme decides how your site looks.

2
00:00:03,241 --> 00:00:07,029
In this video, you open the Themes page, switch the theme of your

3
00:00:07,029 --> 00:00:09,110
site, and turn themes on and off.

4
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:15,481
A theme draws your pages.

5
00:00:15,481 --> 00:00:19,880
It sets the layout, the colors, and the fonts, while the content itself

6
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:21,308
stays in your site.

7
00:00:21,308 --> 00:00:25,250
You can change the theme without editing a single page or post.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,892
Some themes also include templates for specific content.

9
00:00:29,892 --> 00:00:35,290
The Blog Theme, for example, has templates for blog posts, categories, and tags.

10
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,720
A site has two themes.

11
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:41,020
The Site theme draws the pages that visitors see.

12
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:45,520
The Admin theme draws the admin, and the sign-in page as well, unless

13
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:49,960
Use site theme for login page is checked in the User Login settings.

14
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:54,733
The recipe you choose during setup sets the first Site theme.

15
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:59,415
Blog uses The Blog Theme, Agency uses The Agency Theme, Coming Soon uses

16
00:00:59,415 --> 00:01:04,098
The Coming Soon Theme, and Software as a Service uses The Default Theme.

17
00:01:04,098 --> 00:01:06,740
Blank site and Headless site set none.

18
00:01:10,982 --> 00:01:13,336
Let's start on the admin home page.

19
00:01:13,336 --> 00:01:18,215
The Customize theme card has a Manage themes button that opens the Themes page.

20
00:01:18,215 --> 00:01:21,832
The same page is in the admin menu, under Design, Themes.

21
00:01:22,314 --> 00:01:23,741
Click Manage themes.

22
00:01:23,741 --> 00:01:27,251
The Themes page shows a card for each theme you can apply.

23
00:01:27,251 --> 00:01:31,530
The current themes come first, marked This is the current Site theme and

24
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:33,614
This is the current Admin theme.

25
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:38,419
Each card shows a thumbnail, the name of the theme, and a description.

26
00:01:38,419 --> 00:01:43,270
Below them are the author, the website, the tags, and the version of the theme.

27
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:47,578
A theme tagged Admin is an admin theme, such as The Admin Theme.

28
00:01:47,578 --> 00:01:51,342
Make Current on an admin theme sets the Admin theme, and on any

29
00:01:51,342 --> 00:01:53,579
other theme it sets the Site theme.

30
00:01:54,038 --> 00:01:58,431
The other cards are The Agency Theme, The Coming Soon Theme, The Default

31
00:01:58,431 --> 00:02:03,050
Theme, and Safe Mode Theme, which describes itself as a fail-safe theme when

32
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:05,078
no other themes are available.

33
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:11,673
First, let's see the site as it is.

34
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:15,539
On the Themes page, click the Visit Site icon in the top bar.

35
00:02:15,539 --> 00:02:17,847
The home page uses The Blog Theme.

36
00:02:18,299 --> 00:02:21,356
Back on the Themes page, find The Default Theme.

37
00:02:21,356 --> 00:02:25,714
It is disabled, so Orchard Core enables it when you click Make Current.

38
00:02:25,714 --> 00:02:30,299
Two messages confirm that it was enabled and set as the default Site theme.

39
00:02:30,753 --> 00:02:34,743
The card of The Default Theme shows This is the current Site theme,

40
00:02:34,743 --> 00:02:36,438
and its buttons are gone.

41
00:02:36,438 --> 00:02:39,773
The Blog Theme offers Make Current and Disable instead.

42
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:42,466
Open the site again with Visit Site.

43
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:44,490
Make Current changes no content.

44
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:47,739
The layout and the styling come from The Default Theme.

45
00:02:52,009 --> 00:02:56,177
On the Themes page, go back by clicking Make Current on The Blog Theme.

46
00:02:56,177 --> 00:03:00,019
It is already enabled, so one message confirms that it was set as

47
00:03:00,019 --> 00:03:01,589
the default Site theme.

48
00:03:02,109 --> 00:03:03,918
Disable switches a theme off.

49
00:03:03,918 --> 00:03:06,347
Let's click Disable on The Default Theme.

50
00:03:06,347 --> 00:03:10,379
A message confirms it, and the card then offers Enable, which switches a

51
00:03:10,379 --> 00:03:12,499
theme on without making it current.

52
00:03:12,969 --> 00:03:17,386
A current theme has no Make Current, Enable, or Disable button, so this

53
00:03:17,386 --> 00:03:20,943
page does not let you switch off a theme that is in use.

54
00:03:20,943 --> 00:03:23,869
Choose another theme with Make Current first.

55
00:03:28,115 --> 00:03:31,919
At the bottom of the page, the Reset current themes box has two

56
00:03:31,919 --> 00:03:34,896
buttons, Reset Site Theme and Reset Admin Theme.

57
00:03:34,896 --> 00:03:38,535
The box says they are used for sites that can't use theming.

58
00:03:39,006 --> 00:03:42,770
Each button asks you to confirm, and then clears the Site theme or

59
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:46,325
the Admin theme, until you choose one again with Make Current.

60
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:48,626
Leave them alone unless you need them.

61
00:03:52,826 --> 00:03:57,093
Only users with the Apply a Theme permission can open the Themes page.

62
00:03:57,093 --> 00:03:59,732
The Administrator role has it by default.

63
00:03:59,732 --> 00:04:04,056
To give it to another role, edit that role under Access Control, Roles.

64
00:04:06,056 --> 00:04:08,211
Themes decide how your site looks:

65
00:04:08,211 --> 00:04:12,629
under Design, Themes, you choose the Site theme with Make Current and switch

66
00:04:12,629 --> 00:04:15,215
themes on and off with Enable and Disable.

67
00:04:15,215 --> 00:04:16,616
Thanks for watching.

